*Draft, 30 Oct. This is a starting point, not a plan we have agreed. It **can and should change** as the analysis
lands, after Check-in 3 feedback, and after every dry run. Edit it freely; git keeps the history.*

*No numbers are typed here on purpose (CLAUDE.md: never type a number into a doc by hand). Each slide names the
`outputs/` file or doc its number should come from. Items marked **(not built yet)** depend on work still open in
[STATUS.md](../STATUS.md).*

## The format

- 15 minutes, then 10 minutes of questions. 12 to 15 slides, plus a backup appendix that does not count
  ([brief §7](../../reference/01_Student_Brief.md#7-what-you-submit)).
- Audience: a Chief Data Officer and their leadership team.
- Every member speaks. Expect a live record-level trace and an assumption change during Q&A.
- Rough budget: about 1 minute per slide, and 3 minutes for the dashboard demo.

## The thesis (one sentence)

**Agreement isn't proof.** Downstream checks can't catch a defect that came in upstream, because every later check
compares it with something carrying the same mistake. So the controls have to sit where the data enters.

Every slide should support this sentence or be cut.

